  (text "04-LORA: Ra-02 433 MHz, inherited from antenna-controller-rev-c sheet 03-lora (pin map identical: FSPI GPIO10 NSS, 11 MOSI, 12 SCK, 13 MISO; DIO0 GPIO14, DIO1 GPIO21, RST GPIO15)."
    (at 25.4 30.48 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "61f54b16-7cef-44c5-935e-78439f3e32c0")
  )
  (text "FITTED (owner Q3): Ra-02 on the board exactly as rev-c so the project can grow into LoRa; Wi-Fi stays the report path. Firmware puts the SX1278 to sleep while LoRa is unused."
    (at 25.4 34.29 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "336bab3f-9c2a-44cb-8192-955a78c1010d")
  )
  (text "NRESET: no board resistor (SX1278 NRESET floats during POR); firmware: GPIO15 input (high-Z); reset = drive low >= 100 us, then input again, wait 5 ms (Semtech SX1276/77/78/79 7.2.2).\nNSS 10k pull-up (R401). SPI start 4 MHz, max 10 MHz. Never transmit without antenna or 50 ohm load; +20 dBm only after VSWR <= 3:1 is proven.\nFirmware must put the SX1278 into Sleep (0.2 uA) when unused: after POR it idles in Standby (about 1.6 mA), which would dominate the board standby budget."
    (at 25.4 160.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "461db68f-b635-49b8-849e-c86537c16237")
  )
